Keeps this directory present in a fresh clone — tauri.conf.json's bundle.resources references it
by path, and Tauri validates that path exists on EVERY cargo build (not just `cargo tauri build`'s
actual bundling step), so a missing directory breaks plain `cargo build`/`cargo test` too, not just
a release build. The real content (native_module_host.exe) is populated by prepare-bundle.ps1 right
before packaging — see that script's own header comment. This file itself is never read by anything.
